    "explanation": "Rider: your claim is that the trip ran 13.2 km against the 10.0 km route shown at booking and you were charged SGD 19.32. The 13.2 km figure is not in dispute — EV-GPS-02837 records 13.2 km over 104 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps, and POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing distance. What decides the case is that the destination changed mid-trip. Your own chat message at 2026-08-16 17:03:32 (EV-CHAT-02837) reads 'actually can you drop me at the other building, i changed the pin', and EV-TRIP-02837 carries dropoff_amended_at 2026-08-16T17:04:12 together with a stored amended_optimal_distance_km of 13.4 km. POL-RD-05 therefore requires the POL-RD-01 test to be re-run against the amended endpoints using that stored field, and it forbids me from deriving a substitute figure. The arithmetic is 13.2 km − 13.4 km = −0.2 km: there is no excess at all, no deviation survives the recomputation, and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION. The 3.2 km / 32.0% excess shown in the trace data is measured against the superseded 10.0 km booked optimal; it is not the governing comparison. Your SGD 4.50 is not refunded. Driver: your statement that the rider moved the drop-off pin during the trip is corroborated by the chat log and by the dropoff_amended_at timestamp, and the amended baseline of 13.4 km exceeds the 13.2 km actually driven, so no deviation is found against you. Turning to the remaining points the advocates raised: POL-RD-05 / POL-RD-01 (driver and rider) — accepted, and it is the ground of this ruling. POL-RD-01 / POL-RD-06 (rider's fallback that the booked-baseline excess of 3.2 km / 32.0% is an ordinary established deviation warranting the POL-RD-02 refund of 19.32 − 16.02 = 3.30) — rejected: it uses the wrong baseline, because POL-RD-05 resets the optimal to the amended 13.4 km. POL-RD-04 (rider-requested detour) — the instruction is from the rider and is timely, but chat_message.waypoint_hint is null and no road is named, so the 200 m corroboration test cannot be run and that limb is unavailable; it is not needed, as POL-RD-05 disposes. POL-RD-07 — accepted: with zero gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, a 10 s sampling interval and no >500 m jump, the trace is not impaired under limbs (a)–(c), so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. POL-RD-06 — accepted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1/237 completed_trips_90d is far below 0.05, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and no conduct referral or full-refund uplift follows. POL-RD-08 — accepted: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so no corroboration uplift applies. POL-RD-09 — accepted: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02837) shows no ERP gantries and no airport surcharge, so there is no pass-through correction and no billing-integrity referral. The rider's POL-GEN-03 / POL-RD-02 point that payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 is noted but is not itself a ground for a refund: NO_ACTION is party-relative and leaves those fields exactly as they are. Two traffic-advisory claims were discarded by the referee because they cited EV-ADVIS-02837-01 (MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0) without naming its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code; in any event no surviving claim relies on a traffic cause, and under POL-RD-13 an uncited traffic excuse is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. Profile fields rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, prior_disputes_filed and prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and decided nothing. No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fired: the identifiers all match, the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree, no charge line is unmatched, and the excursion is not contradictory evidence because the chat log and the trip record both support the amendment. No clause produces a referral. Confidence is 0.92: the deciding facts — the drop-off amendment and the 13.2 km trace distance — are carried by EV-TRIP-02837 and EV-GPS-02837, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the MISSING advisory at weight 0.0 carries nothing here. The monetary effect is nil, which is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00."
