ed_at timestamp (17:04:12) on EV-TRIP-02837, and the amended baseline has been applied in your favour. No driver compensation is due: the fare ledger charged 13.2 km (distance_charged_km) and the trace records 13.2 km, so there is no unbilled distance under POL-RD-04.\n\nRecord checks. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): no gap exceeds 90 seconds (max_gap_sec 0.0), no jump exceeds 500 m, and the sampling interval is 10 seconds. No repeat-deviation pattern: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 237 (ratio 0.004), below both the 3-flag test and the 0.05 ratio test, so no POL-RD-06 uplift applies and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is produced. The rider's deviation_claims_60d is 0, so the POL-RD-08 corroboration uplift is not triggered; the rider's other profile fields (rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, prior_disputes_filed) and the driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used. The fare ledger shows no ERP gantries and no airport surcharge, so there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) and no referral. No mandatory escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires.\n\nConfidence 0.95, resting on EV-TRIP-02837, EV-GPS-02837 and EV-CHAT-02837, each at weight 1.0. The monetary effect is nil, below the execution threshold. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal within 30 days through the platform's help channel (POL-GEN-04)."
