    "explanation": "Both parties largely agree on the facts that decide this case, and so do I.\n\nTrip TRP-02837 was booked from Blk 55 Lengkok Bahru to Blk 112 Ang Mo Kio Ave 4 (original pin) with a platform optimal route of 10.0 km. During the trip the rider sent an in-app message at 17:03:32 — 'actually can you drop me at the other building, i changed the pin' — and the trip record then shows the drop-off point amended at 17:04:12. That is a drop-off relocation governed by POL-RD-05, which requires the deviation test to be re-run against the optimal route between the amended endpoints. The platform stored that figure on the trip record: trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km = 13.4 km (with amended_optimal_duration_min = 18.5 min). The governing actual distance is the trace figure, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 13.2 km, which POL-RD-01 requires over the rounded trip_record copy. Excess = 13.2 − 13.4 = −0.2 km, i.e. the trip was driven within the amended optimal route. No deviation survives the POL-RD-05 recomputation, and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION where it does not.\n\nThe rider's alternative reading — use the 10.0 km booked figure, giving a 3.2 km / 32.0% excess and a POL-RD-02 refund of $3.30 (charged_total $19.32 less recomputed_fare $16.02) — is rejected. POL-RD-02 runs only once a deviation is established under POL-RD-01, and POL-RD-05 removes the deviation before POL-RD-02 is reached. The rider moved the pin; the additional distance answers the rider's own request, not a driver default.\n\nThe GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 104 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0 and no straight-line jump over 500 m, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) are not met. Because the trace is unimpaired, no independent corroboration is required, the deviation (were one established) would rest on the trace as measured, and no escalation under POL-RD-10(3) arises.\n\nThe rider's chat instruction also satisfies POL-RD-04(a) and (b), but the 200 m corroboration test in POL-RD-04(c) cannot be run because chat_message.waypoint_hint is null; the clause is unavailable on the record (POL-RD-14), and nothing turns on it because POL-RD-05 already governs the amendment. The driver's account that the rider moved the pin is itself corroborated by the chat log and the dropoff_amended_at timestamp, so the driver is not charged with the distance driven to the amended point.\n\nNo billing-integrity defect exists: the fare ledger shows no ERP gantry charges and no airport surcharge, and the $19.32 total reconciles to its itemised lines, so POL-RD-09(4) produces neither a refund nor a referral. No repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 1 (below the 3-flag threshold) and 1/237 completed_trips_90d = 0.004 (below 0.05), so POL-RD-06 does not fire and no driver-conduct referral is made. The rider's profile (deviation_claims_60d = 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated = 0) does not trigger the POL-RD-08 corroboration uplift. Profile fields that POL-GEN-01 makes context-only (rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, prior_disputes_filed, prior_deviation_flags) were mentioned only to be disclaimed and were not used as grounds of decision.\n\nNo traffic advisory was cited by either party and none is relied on; the missing advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02837-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0) is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, and under POL-RD-13 it neither supplies an excuse nor escalates anything. No exculpatory clause was invoked against a cited-but-absent artifact.\n\nThe result is NO_ACTION: the rider's claim is not supported on this record and the $19.32 charge stands as paid (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The monetary effect is $0.00, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00. This ruling rests on artifacts at weight 1.0."
